# SQL's `NOT LIKE` with `%x%`: DS0105 suggesting `!contains`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT LIKE '%42%'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..53
  PIPELINE@0..52
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..52
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..52
        NAME_REF@26..36
          IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        IDENT@37..40 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
        IDENT@41..45 "LIKE"
        WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
        LITERAL@46..52
          STRING@46..52 "'%42%'"
  WHITESPACE@52..53 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `NOT LIKE` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT LIKE '%42%'
  |                                      ^^^^^^^^ this is SQL's pattern match
  |
  = help: use `!contains`: `customerId !contains '42'`
  = note: `contains` ignores case; `contains_cs` matches case exactly
